script-help-run = Save changes, then run using the selected interpreter. The source is read-only until the task ends.
script-help-debug = Start Bash debugging, or continue from the current stop.
script-help-step = Step over a function, step into it, or run until it returns.
script-help-stop = Stop this script and wait for its child processes to exit.
script-help-breakpoint = Set or remove a breakpoint at the source cursor; clicking the marker column does the same.
script-help-markers = B: breakpoint already hit in this session; ?: pending verification; !: rejected by the debugger and inactive; .: disabled; >: current execution line.
script-help-panes = Move between source, output, variables, call stack, expressions and breakpoints.
script-help-controls = Move between controls in the current pane. Tab still indents in the source editor.
script-help-expression = Examine the entered expression while paused. Execute command runs Bash code explicitly; merely viewing variables does not execute it.
script-help-stdin = In the Output pane, keys and paste go to the script. Ctrl+C interrupts the script.
script-help-vim = Edit with Vim; debugging temporarily uses the ordinary read-only source view, then restores Vim.
script-help-menu = Open the editor menu. Run settings changes the interpreter, arguments and working directory.
